            <ArticleTitle>Chronic effort-induced angina as presentation of a totally occluded left main coronary artery: a case report and review.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>382-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/0003319708314247</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In this report, the case of a 40-year-old patient with chronic total occlusion of the left main coronary artery is discussed. Total occlusion of the left main coronary artery is a rare finding at coronary angiography. When present, patients most often have extensive collateral circulation from the right coronary artery. The mainstay of treatment is surgical with coronary artery bypass grafting.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
